","At current returns, reinvesting 22% of profits supports about 6.3% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 15.1% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 8%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.1x, 4.0% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 21, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.0%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (8 sales, net $15.2M sold).","It returns 5.2% a year to shareholders (5.2% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 1.2% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 17.1% of the float, 3.2 days to cover."],"people":["With about 20,096 employees, each generates about $289K of revenue, 0.8x the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 5.1% a year.","That works out to $28K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.6M (13x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":76,"head":"Watch: LEAN BUY-rated, but no margin of safety; it becomes a buy below $169.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 55, gates 16/25)","ROIC 28.6% vs WACC 10.1%","Revenue grew 11.7%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 0.4x","Piotroski F-score 8/9"],"cons":["Trades 4% above fair value of $199"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety"],"buy_below":169.23,"vc":{"base":199.1,"base_src":"dcf","bear":133.97,"bull":304.41,"alt_median":124.78,"n_alt":2,"gap":0.5956,"dispersion":0.1139,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 60% above the other models' median ($125)"]},"med":{"pe":19.2575,"ev_ebitda":11.198,"pfcf":16.4664,"pb":2.375,"roic":0.1281,"gross_margin":0.3475,"fcf_margin":0.0624,"div_yield":0.0228}},"ticker":"EAT","date":"2026-11-06"}